hypotheses.statement:
If a symmetric $a$-linear form $T$ on $\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}^b V$ satisfies $$\label{eq:diagonal}
 T(P,\ldots,P)=0
 \qquad\text{for every product $P$ of $b$ vectors},$$ then $T=0$.

outputs.exact_statement:
Let $V$ be a finite-dimensional complex vector space, and let $a\ge1$ and $b\ge1$ be integers satisfying $b\ge a(a-1)$. If a symmetric $a$-linear form $T$ on $\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}^b V$ satisfies $$\label{eq:diagonal}
 T(P,\ldots,P)=0
 \qquad\text{for every product $P$ of $b$ vectors},$$ then $T=0$.
